        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "On October 18, a group of young people gathered in a London park. They waited for the signal and then shouted as loudly as they could. This was a “Scream Club” event, created to help "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "participants",
            "ref": "v-participant"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "release",
            "ref": "v-release"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stress",
            "ref": "v-stress"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and feel free."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Scream "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "therapy",
            "ref": "v-therapy"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "originally",
            "ref": "v-originally"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " came from the United States and has recently become very popular on TikTok. During the event, participants first shared what made them feel sad, angry, or lonely. Then they all screamed together. Though it looked unusual, many found it fun and helpful. Some passers-by were surprised to see so many people shouting together in the park."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Most participants were in their twenties. “I didn’t realize how much I was holding in until I screamed,” said one young woman. Mona Sharif, the event organizer, started a TikTok group for the club. Over a thousand people "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "signed up",
            "ref": "v-sign-up"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " within just three days, many of them women. A teacher among them "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "commented",
            "ref": "v-comment"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", “Women are often told to stay calm under pressure. It feels good to finally express our feelings freely.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Through such events, young people find a safe way to let out emotions they usually keep inside, leaving them feeling relaxed and happy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
